{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings","id":586612,"title":"Batman and Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-10T17:38:00-07:00","id":586612,"title":"Batman and Changelings","content":"Anyway, with Arkham Knight recently released, I was thinking about Gotham and how psychological it is in the better Batman stories. In particular Arkham Asylum: A Serious House On Serious Earth, which could be construed as Batman-as-changeling trying to hold on to his Clarity despite being in a nexus of the Mad where the Hedge and the mortal world are one and the same.<br /> <br /> I also remembered a joke I cracked about everyone supernatural in the nWoD being a Batman villain, given the mix of tragedy and horror inherent in all of them. This somehow led to the idea of a bunch of oneriomancers somehow ending up in Gotham, deciding a rogue's life was for them, and reforming as a Renaissance-themed group of dreamweavers who ride around committing psychology-themed crimes in their distinctive car, the Jungdai (when parked, it exists in all garages, but is still secure as it only can be consciously perceived if you have empirical evidence of its existence...such as the bent fender of the guy who thought that space was empty despite his gut telling him otherwise).<br /> <br /> Apart from that, how would you Lost-ify Batman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-10-2015, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T21:03:52-07:00","id":586754,"title":"","content":"Hmm, let get back to you on that. I've mostly just contemplated Arkham's inmates as Slashers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:06:31-07:00","id":586836,"title":"","content":"Batman is without a doubt, a Wizened. The guy feels guilty he couldn't do anything to save his parents, and puts his mind and body through hell for the next 20 or so years in order to reach perfection. His nickname is the World's Greatest Detective, he has mastered over 20 styles of martial arts, has access to military grade hardware, and given enough time, he can study and prepare himself for nearly any scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:40:20-07:00","id":587695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=586836#post586836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batman is without a doubt, a Wizened. The guy feels guilty he couldn't do anything to save his parents, and puts his mind and body through hell for the next 20 or so years in order to reach perfection. His nickname is the World's Greatest Detective, he has mastered over 20 styles of martial arts, has access to military grade hardware, and given enough time, he can study and prepare himself for nearly any scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which kith, though? Lurkglider?<br /> <br /> I've considered what some of the Bat-Rogues would be as changelings...<br /> Poison Ivy: Flowering Elemental or Woodblood Fairest<br /> Killer Croc: Water-Dweller/Gristlegrinder Ogre or Beast<br /> Mr. Freeze: Snowskin Wizened<br /> Mad Hatter: Brewer, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:26:57-07:00","id":587900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=587695#post587695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which kith, though? Lurkglider?<br /> <br /> I've considered what some of the Bat-Rogues would be as changelings...<br /> Poison Ivy: Flowering Elemental or Woodblood Fairest<br /> Killer Croc: Water-Dweller/Gristlegrinder Ogre or Beast<br /> Mr. Freeze: Snowskin Wizened<br /> Mad Hatter: Brewer, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Joker's almost a Fae sometimes, though again, Maniac Slasher fits him best. Maybe I'll start a thread about this on the Hunter boards...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:07:32-07:00","id":587968,"title":"","content":"Build it as a freehold,<br /> <br /> The Bat Court: emotion Fear, Appraoch, the huntsmen must commit an outlandish crime with a familar theme that the changelings can investigate<br /> The Arkham Court: emotion Madness approach, appeal to their insanity in someway<br /> The Bane Court: emotion Ambition approach, the huntsmen must challenge their intellect and cuning<br /> The Falcone Court: emotion greed, approach, the huntsmen must utilize the traditons of the mob<br /> <br /> just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:13:54-07:00","id":588036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=587695#post587695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which kith, though? Lurkglider?<br /> <br /> I've considered what some of the Bat-Rogues would be as changelings...<br /> Poison Ivy: Flowering Elemental or Woodblood Fairest<br /> Killer Croc: Water-Dweller/Gristlegrinder Ogre or Beast<br /> Mr. Freeze: Snowskin Wizened<br /> Mad Hatter: Brewer, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the Mad Hatter utilizes mind control chips placed inside his hats to turn people into his slaves, and he has an unhealthy obsession with Alice in Wonderland. He's probably a Loyalist or maybe even a True Fae, himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scarecrow: Brollachan Wizened<br /> <br /> Firefly: Ifrit Oger, or Fireheart Elemental<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T04:54:57-07:00","id":590148,"title":"","content":"If we're going by the Arkham Continuity.<br /> <br /> Could see the Robins as Enscrolled or pledged Mortal/Nightwatch Hunters. (Although Jason Todd would of been caught and dragged into the hedge to end up a Bridge-Burner or a Summer Court Changeling with low Clarity)<br /> <br /> Barbra Gordon: Enscrolled/Network Zero<br /> GPD: All Enscrolled Mortals ( Facing the things they face day to day)<br /> Deathstroke and Deadshot: Task Force Valkyrie Hunters<br /> <br /> Ra's al Ghu and Talia/ League of Shadows: Ascending Ones (Changeling based: Ra's could definitely be a Fairest 2Ed. With High Wyld)<br /> Lucas Fox/WayneTech: Barrett Commission. (Changeling Based: Wizened)<br /> Hugo Strange: Null Mysteriis or Cherion Group (Changeling Based: Wizened privateer)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":1820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","user":"Nightout","date":". 07-14-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T07:34:03-07:00","id":602896,"title":"","content":"The most important thing: Bruce Wayne doesn't dress up as Batman and pretend to be a grim vigilante. Batman dresses up as billionaire playboy Bruce Wayne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/528-darth-fanboy","name":"Darth Fanboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T23:39:02-07:00","id":603551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darth Fanboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=602896#post602896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most important thing: Bruce Wayne doesn't dress up as Batman and pretend to be a grim vigilante. Batman dresses up as billionaire playboy Bruce Wayne.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some takes, anyway (such as the DC Animated Universe). In others - I'm thinking of a Mark Waid JLA story here - both personae are an essential part of him, and he's dysfunctional without either one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 07-26-2015, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T19:08:09-07:00","id":604393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=587695#post587695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which kith, though? Lurkglider?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to have to say he's a Brollachan. Hell, his slogan is &quot;I am vengeance, I am the night!&quot;<br /> <br /> His entire reason for dressing up as a bat is to strike fear into the hearts of his enemies, and Batman is actually afraid of bats, so he had to conquer his own fear. The first time Batman came back from his self imposed exile, he tried to fight crime as a normal man and almost got himself killed by common street thugs. He needed something to strike fear into their hearts, he needed to become The Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T04:56:58-07:00","id":604597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=603551#post603551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some takes, anyway (such as the DC Animated Universe). In others - I'm thinking of a Mark Waid JLA story here - both personae are an essential part of him, and he's dysfunctional without either one.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of a changeling Batman, though, I'd say billionaire playboy Bruce Wayne is the fetch, using his wealth to hide from what happened to &quot;his&quot; parents rather than attack it like Batman. (This would be a case where the fetch and changeling have made peace, since Bruce Wayne is bankrolling Batman).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:13:41-07:00","id":604634,"title":"","content":"This might be a slight exaggeration, but I heard that the city of Gotham is like 95% crime. Place is a total shit hole, which makes it a perfect cover for the Hedge and all the dangers that dwell there.<br /> <br /> As for Joker being driven mad, there's been speculation in the past that Joker is actually completely sane. Hinted at by both Jason Todd and Batman himself. Joker keeps getting put in Arkham because he's clever enough to make himself appear crazy.<br /> <br /> So I think Joker might actually be a True Fae who goes around turning the people of Gotham into more Changelings. Let's look at the evidence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Harley Quin - She used to be a psychiatrist who tried to help people, but after a few sessions with Joker (or just 1 depending on the source), he warped her into a psychotic clown like himself!<br /> <br /> <br /> Jason Todd - Once he was Batman's side kick, but Joker lured him into a trap and tortured him to death. When he was brought back to life, Jason adopted the mantle of Red Hood, the Joker's previous identity before his chemical bath.<br /> <br /> <br /> Two Face (Dark Knight) - Joker gives Batman a choice of who he wants to save and Batman picks Harvey because he believes his &quot;white knight&quot; attitude is the only honorable way to fight crime. Unfortunately this gets Harvey's girl friend killed and horrendously disfigures him in the process, resulting in him becoming the villain known as Two Face and turning on his former friends.<br /> <br /> <br /> Clayface (The Batman) - Joker developed a chemical that turns the consistency of objects to that of clay, allowing him to reshape it to his own twisted art style. One of Batman's friends (I forgot his name) is accidentally exposed to this chemical when he's taken hostage, turning him into the shapeshifting villain known as Clayface.<br /> <br /> <br /> Commissioner Gordon - Although this was a failed experiment, Joker did try to drive Gordon insane by shooting his daughter in the spine and showing naked pictures of her as he rode bound and gagged through a roller coaster in an abandoned theme park.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure he's got some other trophies on the wall, but these are the ones I can think of off the top of my head for Joker's little abductees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-27-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T19:58:15-07:00","id":608792,"title":"","content":"actually if we're going by Dark Knight Bats wanted to go after the girlfriend, Rachel Dawes, someone he himself Loved, and Joker gave him the location of Harvey instead. So Bruce saves Harvey, but he becomes maimed by the explosion. Meanwhile the Police didn't get inside fast enough and she died....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:40:05-07:00","id":610238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=603551#post603551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In some takes, anyway (such as the DC Animated Universe). In others - I'm thinking of a Mark Waid JLA story here - both personae are an essential part of him, and he's dysfunctional without either one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that story. Still, in his own mind, BATMAN is his True Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:22:44-07:00","id":611403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=608792#post608792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually if we're going by Dark Knight Bats wanted to go after the girlfriend, Rachel Dawes, someone he himself Loved, and Joker gave him the location of Harvey instead. So Bruce saves Harvey, but he becomes maimed by the explosion. Meanwhile the Police didn't get inside fast enough and she died....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Is that what that was? I wondered why he suddenly switched his target; didn't make any sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:00:06-07:00","id":611509,"title":"","content":"Guys! Guys! Hear me out.<br /> <br /> Remember how Batman and Joker almost always take center stage when they show up, and how everyone else usually ends up as a narrative satellite?<br /> <br /> This made me think about making them both True Fae &quot;best friends&quot; that are locked in a really old Feud due to metaphysical force of habit and twisted affection. Let me elaborate a bit.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition, the Seeming is a Badge/Scar Of Agency. So the Gentry only have &quot;Seemings&quot; for the purposes of determining what their Miens look like and what their Affinity Contracts are. They are both good at hiding, lying and scaring people, so they are likely pseudo Darklings. Joker looks like an exaggeration of his usual self: his clothes are even more garish and filthy with old bloodstains, foul chemical gases waft from his lapel-flower, blades poke out of his sleeves and other openings, his smile is practically another Gentry, his skin is paler than Death's, his hair is made of ill, greenish moonlight. Batman becomes Strix-like in appearance, but still humanoid and rippling with might. His armored suit becomes a bunch of floating obsidian plates that are united/shaped like an approximation of muscles.<br /> <br /> According to Equinox Road, changelings that reach Wyrd 10 might start having unbelievably potent dreams of their Durance, gradually dropping in Clarity until they hit rock-bottom. The changeling hears the Gentry calling him back home, does so and becomes one of Them.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Batman&quot; (1989), it was the Joker who created Batman. In &quot;The Killing Joke&quot;, it was Batman who created Joker. This could be reflected in a mystery where players try to figure who Gentrified who in order to have some advantage over them and possibly end their Feud.<br /> <br /> As observed, Gotham would simply not exist in real life. Its crime rates would be unsustainable. Also, Gotham often has this sort of telepathic, dramatically appropriate weather. So let's turn Gotham into a Hedge Town that was built, broken and rebuilt many times by Batman and Joker. Hedge Gotham is like a bar for them: they go there for fun with no strings attached, rather than fighting in their actual Realms for Titles. Batman's Realm is like the Batcave, but with more emphasis on the &quot;cave&quot; part. The hi-tech stuff gets replaced with, I dunno, some kind of bloody <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Magitek\" target=\"_blank\">Magitek</a>? Joker's Realm is like a mercurial, nightmarish combination of circus, carnival, asylum and chemical laboratory.<br /> <br /> The Batfamily and the rest of the Rogues Gallery are probably a mixture of changeling/mortal Loyalists, hobgoblins and less important Gentry. You can portray one or more of them as members of other splats, of course. Whatever works.<br /> <br /> As for the inevitable question of how to portray Bruce Wayne as not-Batman, let's say that evidence points to Bruce being the Fetch that Joker left behind when he kidnapped Batman long ago. Instead of killing Fetch Bruce, Changeling Bruce spares him and gradually turns him into an ally. Fetch Bruce is still an ultra rich technology businessman with hands in various human stocks and even Goblin Markets. All the better to provide the mundane and Token bat-gadgets that Gentry Bruce can't reliably craft anymore.<br /> <br /> To make things even more confusing, let's say there is also an equivalent Fetch Jack for the Gentry Joker.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Compliments? Complaints? I'm all ears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-02-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T05:55:56-07:00","id":613252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=611509#post611509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys! Guys! Hear me out.<br /> <br /> Remember how Batman and Joker almost always take center stage when they show up, and how everyone else usually ends up as a narrative satellite?<br /> <br /> This made me think about making them both True Fae &quot;best friends&quot; that are locked in a really old Feud due to metaphysical force of habit and twisted affection. Let me elaborate a bit.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition, the Seeming is a Badge/Scar Of Agency. So the Gentry only have &quot;Seemings&quot; for the purposes of determining what their Miens look like and what their Affinity Contracts are. They are both good at hiding, lying and scaring people, so they are likely pseudo Darklings. Joker looks like an exaggeration of his usual self: his clothes are even more garish and filthy with old bloodstains, foul chemical gases waft from his lapel-flower, blades poke out of his sleeves and other openings, his smile is practically another Gentry, his skin is paler than Death's, his hair is made of ill, greenish moonlight. Batman becomes Strix-like in appearance, but still humanoid and rippling with might. His armored suit becomes a bunch of floating obsidian plates that are united/shaped like an approximation of muscles.<br /> <br /> According to Equinox Road, changelings that reach Wyrd 10 might start having unbelievably potent dreams of their Durance, gradually dropping in Clarity until they hit rock-bottom. The changeling hears the Gentry calling him back home, does so and becomes one of Them.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Batman&quot; (1989), it was the Joker who created Batman. In &quot;The Killing Joke&quot;, it was Batman who created Joker. This could be reflected in a mystery where players try to figure who Gentrified who in order to have some advantage over them and possibly end their Feud.<br /> <br /> As observed, Gotham would simply not exist in real life. Its crime rates would be unsustainable. Also, Gotham often has this sort of telepathic, dramatically appropriate weather. So let's turn Gotham into a Hedge Town that was built, broken and rebuilt many times by Batman and Joker. Hedge Gotham is like a bar for them: they go there for fun with no strings attached, rather than fighting in their actual Realms for Titles. Batman's Realm is like the Batcave, but with more emphasis on the &quot;cave&quot; part. The hi-tech stuff gets replaced with, I dunno, some kind of bloody <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Magitek\" target=\"_blank\">Magitek</a>? Joker's Realm is like a mercurial, nightmarish combination of circus, carnival, asylum and chemical laboratory.<br /> <br /> The Batfamily and the rest of the Rogues Gallery are probably a mixture of changeling/mortal Loyalists, hobgoblins and less important Gentry. You can portray one or more of them as members of other splats, of course. Whatever works.<br /> <br /> As for the inevitable question of how to portray Bruce Wayne as not-Batman, let's say that evidence points to Bruce being the Fetch that Joker left behind when he kidnapped Batman long ago. Instead of killing Fetch Bruce, Changeling Bruce spares him and gradually turns him into an ally. Fetch Bruce is still an ultra rich technology businessman with hands in various human stocks and even Goblin Markets. All the better to provide the mundane and Token bat-gadgets that Gentry Bruce can't reliably craft anymore.<br /> <br /> To make things even more confusing, let's say there is also an equivalent Fetch Jack for the Gentry Joker.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Compliments? Complaints? I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This sounds really exciting. I would really recommend playing '' who Gentrified who''. Maybe make it mystery players need to solve.<br /> For Bat-Family and Gallery of Rogues-why not make them wisps of batman and Joker? Better to do this with Gallery than Family, because '' conflict'' thing. If Batman is Helped by family or needs to save them, it isn't enough for story to have meaning.<br /> What I would suggest doing with Gotham-make it and True Fae that spends time as Realm, Keeper of both Batman and Joker, which they are unaware of. It manipulates people, but is limited as being place. Conflict in it's story is fact that it is constantly hurt and robbed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T07:47:04-07:00","id":613359,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, would Mister Freeze be some form of Fae Touched? His only reason for being a villain is to save his wife from a terminal illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T16:53:59-07:00","id":616887,"title":"","content":"Just because: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gVok-7tDFF8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gVok-7tDFF8</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:08:11-07:00","id":653046,"title":"","content":"I had another idea: maybe Batman and Joker are different Actors that belong to the same Gentry. Gotham is a Title in Realm form, rather than a Hedge Town. The rest of the Rogues Gallery are too different from each other and independent to be a Wisp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:18:15-07:00","id":653051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/586612-batman-and-changelings?p=653046#post653046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had another idea: maybe Batman and Joker are different Actors that belong to the same Gentry. Gotham is a Title in Realm form, rather than a Hedge Town. The rest of the Rogues Gallery are too different from each other and independent to be a Wisp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering what it usually means when an Other starts fighting itself, that'd be what you call <i>exceptionally bad news.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T10:33:15-07:00","id":662039,"title":"","content":"Never thought I would've found the occasion of posting this old thing but here's my take.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Legend of the Dark City<br /> The Feud around the Dream of Gotham<br /> Premise</b></u><br /> <br /> A powerful group of True Fae emulating/ or hailing from the dreams of the Batman Universe decided to express their need to conflict as a battle between their realms. Their Feud is a complex contract destined to last centuries and to enable the oath-circle to stave off stagnation and destruction for that time. It is important to note that these Fae are not the only ones emulating Batman and his foes, so others can join them or appear in the physical world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Due to the wide popularity of their oneiric spawning ground, these Kindly Ones are very powerful, each has five titles described and most have one or two more active outside the Feud. The Feud itself is manifold; some of its forms are obviously violent, flocks of goblins smashing each other to expand their turf or the Dark King directly confronting one of its rivals Actors. Others are calmer like the quest of the Icy Knight to awaken its lost love or even The Breather will to infect its rival\u2019s domain with fearful memes. The conflict goes up and down based on what makes the most compelling story, titles<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mr Freeze : The Knight Clad in Vestments of Sorrow Winter<br /> Poison Ivy : The Lady of the Thorny Ruins Spring<br /> Bane : The Prince of the Venomous Arena<br /> Scarecrow : The Breather of Fearful Dreams Autumn<br /> <br /> <br /> Joker : The Fool who Paints the Heavens Crimson South<br /> Double-Face : The Double Faced King of Coins West<br /> Penguin : The Bird who Takes Trinkets for Souls East<br /> Al-Gul : The Demon Sovereign with Lazarus\u2019 Face North<br /> <br /> Batman : The Dark King of the City of Dread<br /> <br /> Geography<br /> <br /> For this Feud, the True Fae decided to congregate around the Batman\u2019s Realm (figured by the Wonder tower) and open their borders wide. In practice, that means that, to mortals and changelings visitors rare as they may be, the city is larger than any mortal city with the landscape shifting in accordance to the ruler of the zone. Races of hobgoblins and sentient chimeras serve as servants and gangster and the war while others are purely civilians there for the villains to torment and the heroes to save. Even them, one must remember that the Feud-Stage is not and never has been a city and is even further away from reality than the Umbral reflection of one. Buildings change place in a whim, climate can switch seasons in one moment and each change affects more the mind than the body. <br /> <br /> Characters<br /> <br /> Mr Frezze : The Icy King In the Armor of Mourning<br /> Main Actor : The Tearful Knight Clad In Vestments of Sorrow<br /> Secondary Actor : The Unreachable Lady flying Through the Mist<br /> Prop : The Armor of Mourning<br /> Prop: The Instruments of the Hopeless Surgery<br /> Realm : The Icy Spires of the Forsaken Castle<br /> <br /> Poison Ivy : The Queen of the Forest upon the Ruins<br /> Main Actor : The Lady Clad In Flowers and Tree<br /> Secondary Actor: The Lord of Cats Tireless Hunter.<br /> Wisps : The Protectors of Nature<br /> Prop : The Flower of Black Mercy<br /> Realm : The Thorny Ruins of the Urban Jungle<br /> <br /> To precise according to the old design Appearance/Virtue-Sin/Goal-in-the-Feud/Arc<br /> <br /> The Knight is constantly clad in the armor of mourning which grants him most of his power. He is a durable fighter able to manipulate the physical elements of the Endless Winter to destroy his opponents. The Legend he uses most often is to send his ghostly mate to a rival and try to recover her by all means. The pain he inflicts during his expeditions spread his domain.<br /> <br /> His Lady is his perfect opposite save for their shared link with winter. She\u2019s airy and mystical, light and emotional where he\u2019s physical and intellectual. Her legend is strange, so strange some said she\u2019s but an aspect of the Knight, the lady he cannot save. She wanders in the city affecting hobgoblins with sorrow and despair, preparing them for consumption.<br /> <br /> His realm looks like a forgotten laboratory which could belongs equally to an alchemist or a scientist. By the rules of the Feud , one could turn the place against him but it is difficult. It is there that it creates ice goblins and others beasts to defend his domain.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}